{"ok":true,"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/AP/record/SWS_PER_00116","versions":[{"version_id":"AUTOSAR/AP/record/SWS_PER_00116@rel:R25-11#3d9a9e5b","canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/AP/record/SWS_PER_00116","release":"R25-11","content":"function OpenFileStorage [SWS_PER_00116] Upstream: RS_PER_00001 , RS_PER_00004 , RS_PER_00010 , RS_AP_00119 , RS_AP_00120 , RS_AP_00121 , RS_AP_00127 , RS_AP_00128 , RS_AP_00129 , RS_AP_00135 , RS_AP_00137 , RS_AP_00139 , RS_AP_00144 , RS_AP_00147 , RS_AP_00159 ara::core::Result &lt; SharedHandle &lt; FileStorage &gt; &gt; OpenFileStorage (const ara::core::InstanceSpecifier &amp;fs) noexcept; Opens a File Storage. OpenFileStorage will fail with kResourceBusy when the File Storage is currently being modified by a call from another thread to UpdatePersistency, CleanUpPersistency, ResetPersistency, RecoverAllFiles, or ResetAllFiles. Because multiple threads can access the same File Storage concurrently, the File Storage might not be closed when the SharedHandle returned by this function goes out of scope. It will only be closed when all SharedHandles that refer to the same File Storage went out of scope. Header-Datei #include \"ara/per/file_storage.h\" class mono Scope namespace ara::per class mono Exception-Sicherheit exception safe class mono Thread-Sicherheit thread-safe class mono Parameter (in) th Parameter th Beschreibung td fs td The shortName path of a PortPrototype typed by a PersistencyFile StorageInterface. Rückgabewert th Typ th Beschreibung td ara::core::Result &lt; SharedHandle &lt; FileStorage &gt; &gt; td A Result containing a SharedHandle for the File Storage. In case of an error, it contains any of the errors defined below, or a vendor specific error. Fehler th Fehlercode th Beschreibung td PerErrc ::kStorageNotFound td rollback_semantics Returned if the passed InstanceSpecifier does not match any PersistencyFileStorageInterface configured for this Executable. td PerErrc ::kPhysicalStorageFailure td no_rollback_semantics Returned if access to the physical storage fails. td PerErrc ::kIntegrityCorrupted td rollback_semantics Returned if stored data cannot be read because the structural integrity is corrupted. td PerErrc ::kValidationFailed td rollback_semantics Returned if the validity of stored data cannot be ensured. td PerErrc ::kEncryptionFailed td rollback_semantics Returned if the decryption of stored data fails. td PerErrc ::kResourceBusy td rollback_semantics Returned if CleanUpPersistency, or ResetPersistency is currently being executed, or if RecoverAllFiles or ResetAllFiles is currently being executed for the same File Storage. Also, while Update Persistency is currently being executed, this error is returned when OpenFileStorage is called outside of the callback registered via RegisterApplicationDataUpdateCallback, or if the used Instance Specifier differs from the one provided by the callback. td PerErrc ::kOutOfStorageSpace td no_rollback_semantics Returned if the available physical storage space is insufficient for the files that are added/updated during an implicit update of the File Storage. td PerErrc ::kTooManyFiles td rollback_semantics Returned if the files that are added during an implicit update of the File Storage would exceed the configured maxNumberOfFiles. td PerErrc ::kQuotaExceeded td rollback_semantics Returned if the files that are added/updated during an implicit update of the File Storage would exceed the configured maximum AllowedSize. td PerErrc ::kAuthenticationFailed td rollback_semantics Returned if checking the MAC of stored data fails.","meta":{"trigger_kind":"baseline_sync"},"recorded_at":"2026-09-30T16:43:34+00:00","text_key":"d4060659b325"}],"lifecycle":{"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/AP/record/SWS_PER_00116","is_dropped":false,"first_active_release":"R25-11","last_active_release":"R25-11","dropped_in":[],"first_dropped_release":null,"absent_before":["R19-11","R20-11","R21-11","R22-11","R23-11","R24-11"],"platform_releases":["R19-11","R20-11","R21-11","R22-11","R